From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:44:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 144/162] hjviewer: fixes from the 1.9.0 screen review
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The connection window: the permission tiles flatten (hjvCmTileAspect) where the
1.9 notes leave the grid less height, so no toggle is cut in the English cards;
a staff card drops its "(ID)" line; the caution and P5 boxes sit on the panel's
12 px edge with an 8 px gap above; the recording line names the camera tile.

The gate: a session window's offline text counts a ticket A0 took
(hjv-guest-held) as A1's; a server known to be closed asks no A0 and shows A2
after its refusal; S2 shows its text only once a code is there, is S4's with
S8 (no S11), keeps four English buttons in md; S13 as S12 (md, bold first line);
the phone's text buttons are flush with the text and the copy row is centred.

Desktop: own chat bubbles in primaryFill (ownership by chatModel.me.id), Korean
kept whole, 80 %; Tab skips the ID and password values and hidden tools, and
the ID menu, the password's buttons and the account line draw the ring; the ID
field's English hint fits and its suggestions end at the box's edge; U27 takes
two lines on grid cards and its own lines on a phone; the transfer cards speak
Korean ("완료 · 파일 1/1개 · 471 KB"), name a paused job, show the percentage and
speed beside a thin bar and an error in the danger colour; the empty transfer
panel narrows; sizes lose trailing zeros and dates their seconds; the overwrite
question reads as one sentence with [덮어쓰기], plain for an identical file;
danger confirms carry the warning icon, short ones at sm; the admin button sits
level in its row; the device rows keep a right inset; port forwarding's head is
centred; the recording button is a dot with '녹화 중'.

The CM's imitation check also takes the contact line's words (hjviewer관리자,
hjvieweradministrator); the incoming list says "비밀번호 없이" after the
same-account mark; About has no administrator line without a policy's contact.

Phone: the logged-out account line goes while G3 shows (a chevron otherwise),
the admin intro keeps Korean whole and a user's counts take their own line, the
source link sits under the version, the two sub-screens share one "고급" header,
the file screen says what a running job does and counts in Korean, and the
close question uses the lock line's verb.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
